Patch
-----
The fork adds a `--out/--output/-o` CLI option to es.upm.fi.oeg.oops.Cli
that writes the pitfall report to the given path in RDF/XML (the format
OntoPortal's OopsReport parser consumes), instead of the upstream hard-coded
Turtle output `tstOut.model.ttl`. Upstream behaviour is kept when --out is
omitted. The bundled log4j root level is also lowered from DEBUG to WARN so
runs stay quiet.

Build
-----
JDK:       17 (Docker image maven:3.9-eclipse-temurin-17)
Command:   mvn -B -DskipTests compile jar:jar shade:shade
Output:    target/oops-0.3.0-SNAPSHOT.jar (shaded, Main-Class es.upm.fi.oeg.oops.Cli)

Usage
-----
java -jar bin/oops.jar --input-file <ontology.rdf> --out <report.rdf>
